cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Radiomics on LIDC-IDRI pulmonary nodules: no size-adjusted increment over nodule diameter for malignancy prediction, but a robust increment for predicting radiologist disagreement (grey zone)"
message: "If you use this software or these results, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: dubhe7
    website: "https://github.com/dubhe7"
version: v1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/dubhe7/lidc-nodule-radiomics"
keywords:
  - radiomics
  - lung nodule
  - LIDC-IDRI
  - malignancy prediction
  - radiologist disagreement
  - grey zone
abstract: "Dual-endpoint radiomics study on LIDC-IDRI (302 patients / 602 annotated nodules). Endpoint 1 (negative result): predicting radiologist malignancy scores, radiomic features (AUC 0.975 +/- 0.003) add no size-adjusted increment over log(diameter) (AUC 0.980). Endpoint 2 (positive result): predicting radiologist disagreement (grey zone, score = 3), texture features achieve AUC 0.732 +/- 0.007 versus a diameter baseline of 0.401 (inverted), size-adjusted increment Delta-AUC +0.334 (95% CI +0.259 to +0.410), surviving in both the <=15 mm subgroup (+0.149) and the >=4-annotator subgroup (+0.266). Methods: PyRadiomics 107 features, LASSO-L1 logistic regression, nested cross-validation with patient-level grouping, cluster bootstrap CIs (2000), permutation test (p = 0.010)."
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24531302
